    <item>
      <title>Research</title>
      <link>https://spmbitphys.github.io/research/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://spmbitphys.github.io/research/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div style=&#34;text-align: justify;&#34;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;majorana-physics-in-superconductors&#34;&gt;Majorana Physics in superconductors&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Topological superconductors, as an emergent class of superconducting states, provides an ideal platform for the investigation of topology as well as parity symmetry. They also support the existence of Majorana anyons, quasiparticles that are their own antiparticles, with potential applications in fault-tolerant quantum computation. Low temperature STM/STS are advanced experimental techniques widely used to study topological superconducting states due to their ultrahigh spatial and energy resolution. Our research is focusing on using advanced STM technique, such as Spin-polarized STM, to image the magnetic field response of such anyons in topological superconductor candidates. Further more, we seek the possibility to manipulates Majorana anyons and make fusions with them.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
